      "best": {
        "hypothesis": "Compiling entire symmetric Gram coordinates into adjoint-orbit instructions may reduce cold construction work by eliminating reverse products, repeated symmetry assembly, and runtime canonicalization. No improvement has been measured.",
        "mechanism": "Each pair is relabeled by ascending mode rank, preserving canonical order. Integer CAR reduction compiles only B_i^dagger B_j. Homogeneous charge makes every resulting monomial number conserving, so its adjoint swaps its sorted creation and annihilation groups with positive sign. Off-diagonal compilation sums coefficients within these adjoint orbits, doubling fixed points; diagonal compilation retains one representative per orbit. Instantiation emits both orbit members directly. Structural plans are reused across order-preserving mode relabelings, with exact cancellations removed during compilation.",
        "source": "def gram_accumulate(mapping, key, coefficient):\n    coefficient = mapping.get(key, 0) + coefficient\n    if coefficient:\n        mapping[key] = coefficient\n    elif key in mapping:\n        mapping.pop(key)\n\n\ndef gram_insert(group, label):\n    position = 0\n    while position < len(group) and group[position] < label:\n        position += 1\n    if position < len(group) and group[position] == label:\n        return group, 0\n    sign = 1\n    if (len(group) - position) % 2:\n        sign = -1\n    return group[:position] + (label,) + group[position:], sign\n\n\ndef gram_compile(pattern, diagonal):\n    states = {((), ()): 1}\n    for flag, label in pattern:\n        following = {}\n        for pair, coefficient in states.items():\n            creators, annihilators = pair\n            if flag == 0:\n                inserted, sign = gram_insert(annihilators, label)\n                if sign:\n                    gram_accumulate(following, (creators, inserted), coefficient * sign)\n            else:\n                inserted, sign = gram_insert(creators, label)\n                if sign:\n                    if len(annihilators) % 2:\n                        sign = -sign\n                    gram_accumulate(following, (inserted, annihilators), coefficient * sign)\n                position = 0\n                while position < len(annihilators) and annihilators[position] < label:\n                    position += 1\n                if position < len(annihilators) and annihilators[position] == label:\n                    contracted = annihilators[:position] + annihilators[position + 1:]\n                    sign = 1\n                    if (len(annihilators) - position - 1) % 2:\n                        sign = -1\n                    gram_accumulate(following, (creators, contracted), coefficient * sign)\n        states = following\n        if not states:\n            return (), ()\n    orbits = {}\n    for pair, coefficient in states.items():\n        creators, annihilators = pair\n        if diagonal:\n            if creators <= annihilators:\n                orbits[pair] = coefficient\n        else:\n            if creators == annihilators:\n                coefficient *= 2\n            elif creators > annihilators:\n                pair = (annihilators, creators)\n            gram_accumulate(orbits, pair, coefficient)\n    slots = {}\n    groups = []\n    instructions = []\n    for pair, coefficient in orbits.items():\n        for group in pair:\n            if group not in slots:\n                slots[group] = len(groups)\n                groups.append(group)\n        instructions.append((slots[pair[0]], slots[pair[1]], coefficient))\n    return tuple(groups), tuple(instructions)\n\n\ndef propose(payload):\n    words = [tuple(word) for word in payload['words']]\n    adjoints = [tuple((1 - flag, mode) for flag, mode in reversed(word)) for word in words]\n    plans = payload['cache'].setdefault('symmetric_gram_orbit_plans_v1', {})\n    result = {}\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        for j in range(i, len(words)):\n            product = adjoints[i] + words[j]\n            modes = sorted(set(mode for flag, mode in product))\n            labels = {mode: position for position, mode in enumerate(modes)}\n            pattern = tuple((flag, labels[mode]) for flag, mode in product)\n            key = (i == j, pattern)\n            if key not in plans:\n                plans[key] = gram_compile(pattern, i == j)\n            groups, instructions = plans[key]\n            if instructions:\n                creations = [tuple((1, modes[label]) for label in group) for group in groups]\n                annihilations = [tuple((0, modes[label]) for label in group) for group in groups]\n                coordinate = (i, j)\n                for first, second, coefficient in instructions:\n                    word = creations[first] + annihilations[second]\n                    result.setdefault(word, {})[coordinate] = coefficient\n                    if first != second:\n                        word = creations[second] + annihilations[first]\n                        result.setdefault(word, {})[coordinate] = coefficient\n    return result\n",
        "assumptions": "Words obey CAR, have degree at most three, and share one particle-number charge. Modes are hashable and sortable in the required ascending order. Flags are zero or one. The cache starts empty. All coefficients are constructed using Python integer arithmetic; no oracle or installed helper is required.",
        "failure_cases": "Performance is unmeasured. Pairwise rank compression and cold plan compilation may outweigh savings when structural reuse is low. Plans remain resident for the run, and output construction still requires quadratic coordinate traversal. Mixed-charge dictionaries invalidate the positive-sign adjoint-orbit rule used here.",
