        "hypothesis": "Compiling each symmetric Gram coordinate into adjoint orbits can reduce cold construction work by eliminating the second ordered product and resolving symmetric cancellations before concrete-mode substitution. Performance is unmeasured.",
        "mechanism": "Compile the first-occurrence equality pattern of B_i^dagger B_j using integer CAR insertion. Homogeneous charge guarantees equal creator and annihilator counts in every surviving term, so canonical adjunction simply exchanges the two ascending mode groups with positive sign. For off-diagonal coordinates, fold coefficients into these exchange orbits during compilation, removing cancellations immediately. Instantiate each surviving orbit once and emit its one or two canonical words. Cache only structural plans generated during the current construction.",
        "source": "def gram_add(values, key, coefficient):\n    coefficient += values.get(key, 0)\n    if coefficient:\n        values[key] = coefficient\n    elif key in values:\n        values.pop(key)\n\n\ndef gram_insert(group, label):\n    position = 0\n    while position < len(group) and group[position] < label:\n        position += 1\n    if position < len(group) and group[position] == label:\n        return group, 0\n    sign = 1\n    if (len(group) - position) % 2:\n        sign = -1\n    return group[:position] + (label,) + group[position:], sign\n\n\ndef gram_compile(pattern, symmetric):\n    states = {((), ()): 1}\n    for flag, label in pattern:\n        following = {}\n        for pair, coefficient in states.items():\n            creators, annihilators = pair\n            if flag == 0:\n                inserted, sign = gram_insert(annihilators, label)\n                if sign:\n                    gram_add(following, (creators, inserted), coefficient * sign)\n            else:\n                inserted, sign = gram_insert(creators, label)\n                if sign:\n                    if len(annihilators) % 2:\n                        sign = -sign\n                    gram_add(following, (inserted, annihilators), coefficient * sign)\n                position = 0\n                while position < len(annihilators) and annihilators[position] < label:\n                    position += 1\n                if position < len(annihilators) and annihilators[position] == label:\n                    contracted = annihilators[:position] + annihilators[position + 1:]\n                    value = coefficient\n                    if (len(annihilators) - position - 1) % 2:\n                        value = -value\n                    gram_add(following, (creators, contracted), value)\n        states = following\n        if not states:\n            return (), ()\n    if symmetric:\n        orbits = {}\n        for pair, coefficient in states.items():\n            creators, annihilators = pair\n            if creators == annihilators:\n                gram_add(orbits, pair, 2 * coefficient)\n            elif creators < annihilators:\n                gram_add(orbits, pair, coefficient)\n            else:\n                gram_add(orbits, (annihilators, creators), coefficient)\n        states = orbits\n    slots = {}\n    groups = []\n    instructions = []\n    for pair, coefficient in states.items():\n        creators, annihilators = pair\n        for group in pair:\n            if group not in slots:\n                slots[group] = len(groups)\n                groups.append(group)\n        instructions.append((slots[creators], slots[annihilators], coefficient))\n    return tuple(groups), tuple(instructions)\n\n\ndef gram_substitute(group, modes):\n    ordered = []\n    sign = 1\n    for label in group:\n        ordered.append(modes[label])\n        position = len(ordered) - 1\n        while position > 0 and ordered[position - 1] > ordered[position]:\n            ordered[position - 1], ordered[position] = ordered[position], ordered[position - 1]\n            sign = -sign\n            position -= 1\n    return tuple((1, mode) for mode in ordered), tuple((0, mode) for mode in ordered), sign\n\n\ndef propose(payload):\n    words = payload['words']\n    adjoints = [tuple((1 - flag, mode) for flag, mode in reversed(word)) for word in words]\n    plans = payload['cache'].setdefault('gram_adjoint_orbit_plans_v1', {})\n    result = {}\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        for j in range(i, len(words)):\n            symmetric = i != j\n            labels = {}\n            modes = []\n            pattern = []\n            for word in (adjoints[i], words[j]):\n                for flag, mode in word:\n                    if mode not in labels:\n                        labels[mode] = len(modes)\n                        modes.append(mode)\n                    pattern.append((flag, labels[mode]))\n            key = (symmetric, tuple(pattern))\n            if key not in plans:\n                plans[key] = gram_compile(key[1], symmetric)\n            groups, instructions = plans[key]\n            if not instructions:\n                continue\n            substitutions = [gram_substitute(group, modes) for group in groups]\n            coordinate = (i, j)\n            for creation_slot, annihilation_slot, coefficient in instructions:\n                creation = substitutions[creation_slot]\n                annihilation = substitutions[annihilation_slot]\n                value = coefficient * creation[2] * annihilation[2]\n                word = creation[0] + annihilation[1]\n                result.setdefault(word, {})[coordinate] = value\n                if symmetric and creation_slot != annihilation_slot:\n                    partner = annihilation[0] + creation[1]\n                    result.setdefault(partner, {})[coordinate] = value\n    return result\n",
        "assumptions": "Creation flags are 0 or 1; modes are hashable and consistently orderable. Words satisfy the stated degree bound and homogeneous charge. The supplied cache starts empty. Injective substitution preserves distinct structural terms and exchange orbits, so each emitted coordinate coefficient needs only one assignment.",
